/*!
\page page_stphmdcollection StPhmdCollection — PHMD Collection Documentation

\section phmd_overview Overview

The <b>Photon Multiplicity Detector (PHMD)</b>, also labelled PMD in STAR documentation,
measures photon multiplicity at forward rapidities (2.3 < η < 3.9).  It is a gas-filled
pad detector and consists of two planes facing each other:

- <b>PMD</b> (\c kPhmdId = 26) — the photon-signal plane.  Photons convert in a lead
  absorber and produce electromagnetic showers detected here.
- <b>CPV</b> (\c kPhmdCpvId = 25) — the Charged Particle Veto plane.  Charged particles
  that reach this plane without converting allow rejection of non-photon signals.

\ref StPhmdCollection is the single top-level object saved in \c StEvent for all PHMD data.
It owns two \ref StPhmdDetector objects (one per plane), both of which are heap-allocated in
the constructor.  Cluster data reside one level deeper inside each \ref StPhmdDetector via
an owned \ref StPhmdClusterCollection.

\section phmd_classes Classes in this group

| Class | Role |
|-------|------|
| \ref StPhmdCollection | Top-level event container for both PHMD detector planes |
| \ref StPhmdClusterCollection | Per-plane container for reconstructed PHMD clusters |

Related classes (not documented here):

| Class | Role |
|-------|------|
| \ref StPhmdDetector | One PHMD detector plane (PMD or CPV); holds supermodules and clusters |
| \c StPhmdModule | One supermodule within a detector plane; holds raw hits |
| \ref StPhmdHit | A single cell (pad) hit in a PHMD supermodule |
| \ref StPhmdCluster | A reconstructed cluster of adjacent cells |

\section phmd_ids Detector identifier values

| \c StDetectorId | Integer | Physical plane |
|----------------|---------|----------------|
| \c kPhmdCpvId | 25 | Charged Particle Veto (CPV) |
| \c kPhmdId | 26 | Photon Multiplicity Detector (PMD, photon signal) |

\section phmd_hierarchy Containment hierarchy

\code{.unparsed}
StPhmdCollection                                    (1 per event, in StEvent)
├── mDetector    (StPhmdDetector*, kPhmdId=26,    heap-allocated, created in ctor)
│   ├── mModules (StPhmdModule*, supermodules, heap-allocated by StPhmdDetector)
│   │   └── hits (StSPtrVecPhmdHit — owns StPhmdHit objects)
│   └── mClusters (StPhmdClusterCollection*, heap-allocated, owned by StPhmdDetector)
│       └── mClusters (StSPtrVecPhmdCluster — owns StPhmdCluster objects)
└── mCpvDetector (StPhmdDetector*, kPhmdCpvId=25, heap-allocated, created in ctor)
    ├── mModules (StPhmdModule*, supermodules)
    └── mClusters (StPhmdClusterCollection*)
\endcode

\section phmd_ownership Object Ownership

\subsection phmd_own_coll StPhmdCollection
\c mDetector and \c mCpvDetector are raw pointers to \ref StPhmdDetector objects
heap-allocated in the constructor: \c new \c StPhmdDetector(kPhmdId) and
\c new \c StPhmdDetector(kPhmdCpvId).  The destructor always calls \c delete on both.
\ref StPhmdCollection::setDetector replaces the appropriate slot after deleting the
existing occupant.

\warning Do not delete \ref StPhmdDetector objects obtained from
\ref StPhmdCollection::detector.

\subsection phmd_own_cluster StPhmdClusterCollection
\c mClusters is a \c StSPtrVecPhmdCluster owning vector.  \c StStrArray automatically
deletes \ref StPhmdCluster objects on destruction.  The \ref StPhmdClusterCollection
destructor is an explicit no-op.  Additional methods
\ref StPhmdClusterCollection::deleteCluster and
\ref StPhmdClusterCollection::deleteClusters allow removal during event processing.

\warning Do not delete \ref StPhmdCluster objects obtained from
\ref StPhmdClusterCollection::clusters directly, unless you have first removed them with
\ref StPhmdClusterCollection::deleteCluster.

\section phmd_members Data Members

\subsection phmd_mem_coll StPhmdCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StPhmdDetector* | \c mDetector | PMD photon-signal plane (\c kPhmdId = 26), heap-allocated |
| \c StPhmdDetector* | \c mCpvDetector | CPV charged-veto plane (\c kPhmdCpvId = 25), heap-allocated |

\subsection phmd_mem_cluster StPhmdClusterCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StDetectorId | \c mDetector | Identifier of the detector plane these clusters belong to |
| \c StSPtrVecPhmdCluster | \c mClusters | Owned vector of reconstructed \ref StPhmdCluster objects |
| \c Int_t | \c mClusterFinderId | Cluster-finder algorithm identifier |
| \c Int_t | \c mClusterFinderParamVersion | Version of the cluster-finder parameter set |

\section phmd_methods Key Methods

\subsection phmd_meth_coll StPhmdCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c StPhmdDetector* \c detector(StDetectorId) | PMD or CPV detector plane; \c nullptr for any other ID |
| \c const \c StPhmdDetector* \c detector(StDetectorId) \c const | Const overload |
| \c void \c setDetector(StPhmdDetector*) | Replace a plane (PMD or CPV) based on \c val->id(); deletes the existing pointer |

\subsection phmd_meth_cluster StPhmdClusterCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c int \c numberOfclusters() \c const | Number of clusters in the collection |
| \c StSPtrVecPhmdCluster& \c clusters() | Mutable reference to the cluster vector |
| \c const \c StSPtrVecPhmdCluster& \c clusters() \c const | Read-only reference |
| \c void \c addCluster(StPhmdCluster*) | Append a cluster (takes ownership) |
| \c void \c deleteCluster(StPhmdCluster*) | Remove (and delete) a specific cluster |
| \c void \c deleteClusters() | Remove (and delete) all clusters |
| \c int \c clusterFinderId() \c const | Cluster-finder algorithm identifier |
| \c int \c clusterFinderParamVersion() \c const | Cluster-finder parameter version |
| \c void \c setClusterFinderId(int) | Set cluster-finder algorithm identifier |
| \c void \c setClusterFinderParamVersion(int) | Set cluster-finder parameter version |

\section phmd_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
// Access PHMD cluster collections
const StPhmdCollection* phmdColl = event->phmdCollection();
if (!phmdColl) return;

// Photon-signal plane (PMD)
const StPhmdDetector* pmd = phmdColl->detector(kPhmdId);
if (pmd) {
    const StPhmdClusterCollection* clColl = pmd->cluster();
    if (clColl) {
        for (const StPhmdCluster* cl : clColl->clusters()) {
            // cl->eta(), cl->phi(), cl->energy(), cl->numberOfCells(), etc.
        }
    }
}

// Charged-veto plane (CPV)
const StPhmdDetector* cpv = phmdColl->detector(kPhmdCpvId);
if (cpv) {
    const StPhmdClusterCollection* clColl = cpv->cluster();
    if (clColl) {
        for (const StPhmdCluster* cl : clColl->clusters()) {
            // use CPV cluster information for charged-particle veto
        }
    }
}

// Raw cell hits in the PMD (supermodule loop)
if (pmd) {
    for (unsigned int iMod = 0; iMod < pmd->numberOfModules(); ++iMod) {
        const StPhmdModule* mod = pmd->module(iMod);
        if (!mod) continue;
        // iterate over mod->hits() for cell-level data
    }
}
\endcode

*/
